<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 50 bln lire of Italy Cct.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 50 bln lire of Italy Cct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 50 billion lire of seven-year variable-rate certificates (CCT) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 700 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 8.65 trillion lire at the open auction for the September 1, 2003 paper against 7.0 trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 101.30 from 101.45 at the previous CCT sale on September 16.</p>
</text>
